 "title": "How to Speak Like a Politician",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This video breaks down three core rules used by politicians to deliver powerful speeches and influence large crowds. The creator shares practical public speaking techniques, including smiling gently, keeping mouth muscles expanded, and using pauses effectively.",
 "key_points": [
  "Rule number one: Smile more, let yourself free, and pass a gentle smile while talking to make people feel warm and appear more believable.",
  "Rule number two: The muscles of your mouth should constantly be expanding and not contracting; do not speak as if you are sharing a secret.",
  "Rule number three: Take more pauses, because when you take enough pauses, people tend to believe that you know what you are talking about."
 ],
 "content": "How are political speeches so powerful that they can influence people at such a large scale? Ladies and gentlemen, welcome to episode one of how to speak like a politician. Rule number one: You need to smile more. Let yourself free and pass a gentle smile while you are talking. Why? Because it makes people feel you're warm, it makes you more believable. Rule number two: The muscles of your mouth should constantly be expanding and not contracting. Don't speak like this, you are not sharing a secret. Rule number three: Take more pauses, because when you take enough pauses, people tend to believe that you know what you are talking about. Follow for part two.\n\nText on screen:\nHOW TO SPEAK LIKE A POLITICIAN? Part 1\nZOHRAN NEW YORK CITY\nFollow For Part 2! Out Tomorrow!",
